{"name":"Indian Paintbrush","hex":"#fa9761","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"indian","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Indian (“indigene”)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Indian (“indigenous”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indian"},{"term":"paintbrush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thin brush for applying paint."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paintbrush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Indian Paintbrush (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Indian Paintbrush Productions LLC is an American film production company founded by businessman Steven Rales in 2006. It is based in Santa Monica, California, and specializes in the production and distribution of comedy-drama and romantic films. Rales and Indian Paintbrush have financed and produced several releases by filmmaker Wes Anderson, such as The Grand Budapest Hotel (2014), Isle of Dogs (2018), and The Wonderful Story of Henry Sugar (2023). Other notable productions include Like Crazy (2011), Me and Earl and the Dying Girl (2015), and Conclave (2024)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Paintbrush_(company)","wikidata":"Q17415951"},{"title":"Indian Paintbrush Book Award","blocks":[{"text":"The Indian Paintbrush Book Award is an award given annually to books nominated and voted on by children in the fourth, fifth, and sixth grades in Wyoming. The award was first given in 1986. The award is sponsored by the Wyoming Library Association and the Wyoming State Reading Council."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Paintbrush_Book_Award","wikidata":"Q6021201"},{"title":"Paintbrush","blocks":[{"text":"A paintbrush is a brush used to apply paint or ink. A paintbrush is usually made by clamping bristles to a handle with a ferrule. They are available in various sizes, shapes, and materials. Thicker ones are used for filling in, and thinner ones are used for details. They may be subdivided into decorators' brushes used for painting and decorating and artists' brushes used for visual art."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Paintbrushes.jpg/330px-Paintbrushes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paintbrush","wikidata":"Q193897"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png/120px-Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png/120px-Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brush parts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParts_of_a_Paintbrush.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Brush_Handles.jpg/500px-Brush_Handles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Brush_Handles.jpg/1280px-Brush_Handles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Brush_Handles.jpg/500px-Brush_Handles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brush handle styles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrush_Handles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg/500px-Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg/1280px-Decorators%27paintbiushes.jpg?utm_s